This is a solid foundation, but there are **six bugs and four missing features** that need to be addressed before selling it. Here's a complete audit and the upgraded `App.jsx`.

***

## Critical Bugs

| # | Issue | Why it Hurts | Fix |
|---|-------|-------------|-----|
| 1 | `Settings`, `Chat`, `Inbox` defined **inside** `App` | React destroys + remounts them on every render, wiping focus and causing flicker [1][2] | Move them outside `App`, pass state as props |
| 2 | `textarea` has no auto-resize | Feels broken after line 1 [3] | `useAutoResize` hook using `scrollHeight` |
| 3 | `showMenu` state is declared and set but **never rendered** | Dead code; "Clear Chat" is unreachable | Wire a real context menu in Chat header |
| 4 | `clearChat` is defined but **never exposed** in UI | Users can't clear history | Add to header kebab menu |
| 5 | Auto-scroll always fires | Scrolls user back to bottom while they're reading history | Track `atBottom` ref, only follow if within 80px |
| 6 | OpenClaw WS never reconnects on drop | Single disconnection ends the session forever | Add `onclose` retry with 5s backoff |

***

## Missing Features for a $10 Product

- **Markdown rendering** — Bot responses use code blocks, bold, lists constantly; raw text is unusable
- **Message context menu** — Right-click → Copy / Delete (expected in any chat app)
- **Add / Delete bots** — Users need to point at their own agent, not just edit two hardcoded ones
- **Smart unread badge cap** — Shows raw count; should cap at `9+`

